  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\rLocation and Block Plan - 2104-FLT-E01-00\rProposed Floor Plan - 2104-FLT-P02-00\rProposed Elevations Plan - 2104-FLT-P03-00\rProposed Side Elevation Plan - 2104-FLT-P03-01\rProposed Section Plan - 2104-FLT-P04-00\rFlood Evacuation Plan\rFlood Risk Assessment\rDaylight and Sunlight Assessment\rFlush Flooding document \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of the 2 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rThese details should demonstrate: \rLocation: Near entrances or main access \rDesign: Stands or wall bars \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit \rCoverage: Covered where possible \rAccessibility: Step-free, no obstructions \r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024), shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The residential unit hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of sound insulation measures between the proposed ground floor residential accommodation and adjoining accommodation above have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning\rAuthority. The submitted details shall demonstrate how the development will protect future occupiers from noise transmission arising from neighbouring activities. The approved measures shall be fully implemented prior to first occupation of the residential unit and shall be retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To protect the amenities of future occupiers and ensure an acceptable standard of residential accommodation.\r"
  ],
